{"_id":"6a2ffb2c2204ffbc59e5a8ff","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"LERo7-ggtfZ-KZyNdBwt6","description":"# Airflow\n\nApache Airflow is an open-source platform for authoring, scheduling, and monitoring data pipelines. Pipelines are defined as DAGs (Directed Acyclic Graphs) in Python, where each node is a task and edges define dependencies. Airflow provides a web UI for monitoring runs, retrying failures, and tracking execution history. It is the standard orchestration tool for production Python data pipelines.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Airflow 101: Building Your First Workflow","url":"https://airflow.apache.org/docs/apache-airflow/stable/tutorial/fundamentals.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb14"},{"type":"article","title":"Introduction to Apache Airflow","url":"https://www.dataquest.io/blog/introduction-to-apache-airflow/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb15"},{"type":"video","title":"Airflow Tutorial For Beginners (2026)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IiczxlbQb8s","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb16"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T13:16:28.608Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/LERo7-ggtfZ-KZyNdBwt6.md"}